<title>INDIA: India's SRF 1st half net falls sharply.</title>
<headline>India's SRF 1st half net falls sharply.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to end-September</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	  87.4 vs   236.3</p>
<p>    Operating profit     913.6 vs   639.0</p>
<p>    Net sales	    2,856.1 vs 2,303.9</p>
<p>NOTE - Indian tyre cord, chemicals and lenses company SRF Ltd said in a statement that pre-tax profit fell because of higher interest costs. It said the firm was finalising a plan to strengthen its financial structure to bring down the interest burden, which it said was 590.2 million rupees against 277.5 million in the previous year.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
